              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "camīnus, camīnī — \"a forge, a furnace; a fireplace\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In camīnō ignis magnus ardet. A big fire burns in the forge."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, masculine: camīnus, camīnī m. A smith's forge, or a stove for heating a room. English chimney comes from a word built on it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "camīnus was borrowed from Greek kamīnos 'furnace' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English chimney comes, through French, from Late Latin camīnāta, built on it."
            }
          ]
        },
